#: manual/index.md:1
msgid "err_marker"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:5
msgid "This manual documents version `v0.1.3` of `KCN-judu/err_marker`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:7
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:9
msgid "`err_marker` shows a reader where an error is. It renders a sequence (the command-line arguments of a program, a list of tokens, or a string), draws a line of markers under the part that is wrong, and prints a message below:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:19
msgid "The library is one package with two types and four functions. It does not read files, track line numbers or colour its output; it turns a sequence, a position and a message into three lines of text."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:23
msgid "The 0.1 series has known limits with non-ASCII text; they are listed in the [design](design/core.md) and tracked for 0.2.0 in [#5](https://github.com/moonbit-community/err_marker/issues/5)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:27
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:33
msgid "Then import `\"KCN-judu/err_marker\"` in your `moon.pkg`; the package is available as `@err_marker`. The module needs the MoonBit toolchain 0.10 or later (`moonc` ≥ 0.10) and depends on `moonbitlang/core` and, for the `error_report` adapter only, `marianoguerra/error-report`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:38
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#: manual/index.md:40
msgid "The module has three public packages: the root package at `src`, documented as `core`; `src/cursor`, documented as `cursor`; and `src/error_report`, documented as `error_report`."
msgstr ""

